{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0a53cf241116eec7a3931b689b20462069c7b9f7a73b6f829474b879b176ed18","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion verifier","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:116","src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json:26,49","src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:224","tests/unit/test_audit_completion_v2.py","tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page_heldout.py","completion-verifier eval spec"],"problem_keywords":["completion verdict","kind field","schema update","non-codebase","verifier prompt","backward compatibility"],"propositions":["The completion verifier emits a `kind` field with an unconstrained string type that currently lacks enum validation, causing silent mismatches if reader and emitter disagree on allowed values.","The `kind` field value must change from the current value to one of two valid values: `codebase-verifiable` or `non-codebase`.","The verifier prompt, contracts.py, and completion_verdict.schema.json must all specify the same set of allowed `kind` values to avoid silent rendering failures.","Old records with `operator-attested` kind value must continue to render correctly after the schema change to support backward compatibility.","The change is blocked until S2 is complete; the reader must accept both old and new kind values before the emitter switches to prevent audit page mis-rendering."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787603668321486001,"uuid":"de898adb-a066-461c-8655-f6669e8b3812"}